      "writtenOn": "2017-01-11T15:57:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah - this seems like it would be something to add to the validation pieces at the beginning of this method. That way if the role in a mapping belongs to a different domain than the identity provider, we can bail before we create anything.\n\nOn the other hand, emitting that kinda of error at authentication time might not help the user that much. If anything I would think we\u0027d want to have that kind of validation when the operator originally creates the mapping so that users don\u0027t have to deal with an exception they can\u0027t do anything about, that could be a future improvement though.",
